    q: 'What is the MC2R receptor?',
    a: 'MC2R is the receptor for ACTH on the adrenal cortex. When ACTH from the pituitary binds it, the adrenal gland makes cortisol. It is the final receiving step of the body’s stress-hormone (HPA) axis and, unusually, responds to ACTH alone.',
